e. Instead, I should create a shared error-reporting helper class that each logger can use to report failures consistently, then update the catch blocks in all the loggers to call this helper instead of just logging errors. The main service will post a Toast notification and the main activity will listen for these EventBus events to display them to the user.\n\nFor implementation, I'll focus on the loggers most likely to hit permission issues: GPX, KML, CSV, and GeoJSON. I need to add a `FileWriteError` event to ServiceEvents and set up a helper mechanism for error reporting across all the file logging classes. I'm realizing the scope here—there are many logger classes to modify, but the most impactful changes are at the service level and for the most common file formats like GPX and KML, since CSV already propagates errors synchronously. Let me check what Toast strings are available in the app to see if there's already an error message I can reuse rather than adding a new string resource.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
