{"type":"assistant","uuid":"0acfaf77-b30f-4ca6-8363-b99476b8549d","session_id":"27a7e77e-d6f8-4f91-a58e-a8a95b3ec8ae","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"0acfaf77-b30f-4ca6-8363-b99476b8549d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete. Here's a summary of all changes made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### Bug Fixed\nGPSLogger was silently swallowing file write errors (e.g., permission denied), causing data loss without the user ever knowing.\n\n### Root Cause\nTwo layers of error swallowing:\n1. **Async loggers** (GPX, KML, GeoJSON, NMEA) caught exceptions in background threads and only logged to SLF4J\n2. **Top-level `writeToFile()`** caught sync errors (e.g., CSV) and also only logged to SLF4J\n\n### Files Modified (8 files)\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `ServiceEvents.java` | Added `FileWriteError` EventBus event class |\n| `strings.xml` | Added `file_write_error` user-facing message |\n| `GpsLoggingService.java` | Added Toast + EventBus post for sync file errors |\n| `GpsMainActivity.java` | Added `onEventMainThread(FileWriteError)` handler showing Toast |\n| `Gpx10FileLogger.java` | Added EventBus post in write/annotate error handlers |\n| `Kml22FileLogger.java` | Added EventBus post in write/annotate error handlers |\n| `GeoJSONWriterPoints.java` | Added EventBus post in error handler |\n| `NmeaFileLogger.java` | Replaced empty catch blocks with EventBus post |\n\n### How It Works\n- When any logger's file write fails, it posts a `ServiceEvents.FileWriteError` event via EventBus\n- `GpsMainActivity` listens for this event and shows a `Toast` notification\n- The main activity also shows a Toast for synchronous errors caught in `writeToFile()`\n- SLF4J logging is preserved for debugging\n\n### Patch Location\n`fix.patch` — 226 lines, covers all 8 modified files."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81038,"output_tokens":411,"cache_read_input_tokens":80256,"total_tokens":81449}}}
